ler is the first candle? How much more, or how much taller, means find the gap. Line up the two bars. Count the extra pieces: one, two, three, four, five. The first candle is five-sevenths of a foot taller. We found the gap, so we took away. We did not add. Watch out! Check if your answer can be simpler. One-twelfth plus one-twelfth is two-twelfths. Two twelfths fit exactly under one sixth. So the simplest form is one-sixth."}, "vid-close": {"words": [{"text": "Read", "type": "word", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.32}, {"text": "the", "type": "word", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.4}, {"text": "whole", "type": "word", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.72}, {"text": "story,", "type": "word", "start": 0.8, "end": 1.68}, {"text": "find", "type": "word", "start": 1.76, "end": 2.0}, {"text": "the", "type": "word", "start": 2.04, "end": 2.08}, {"text": "clue", "type": "word", "start": 2.16, "end": 2.4}, {"text": "words,", "type": "word", "start": 2.48, "end": 3.2}, {"text": "then", "type": "word", "start": 3.32, "end": 3.44}, {"text": "do", "type": "word", "start": 3.56, "end": 3.68}, {"text": "one", "type": "word", "start": 3.76, "end": 3.92}, {"text": "step", "type": "word", "start": 4.0, "end": 4.24}, {"text": "at", "type": "word", "start": 4.32, "end": 4.4}, {"text": "a", "type": "word", "start": 4.453, "end": 4.507}, {"text": "time.", "type": "word", "start": 4.56, "end": 5.24}, {"text": "Now", "type": "word", "start": 5.52, "end": 5.68}, {"text": "it's", "type": "word", "start": 5.72, "end": 5.92}, {"text": "your", "type": "word", "start": 6.04, "end": 6.16}, {"text": "turn!", "type": "word", "start": 6.36, "end": 6.8}], "text": "Read the whole story, find the clue words, then do one step at a time. Now it's your turn!"}, "words": {"words": [{"text": "Altogether.", "type": "word", "start": 0.0, "end": 1.04}, {"text": "...", "type": "word", "start": 1.28, "end": 1.36}, {"text": "How", "type": "word", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.52}, {"text": "much", "type": "word", "start": 1.6, "end": 1.84}, {"